# Annotation SCC ordering — NEGATIVE test
# Use @MyType before declaring MyType, with @MyType in a SEPARATE dict (not the same letrec group).
# Should fail with "undefined type: MyType".
#
# This is the negative complement to annotation_scc_ordering.llt-eval — verifies that
# the SCC dependency tracking actually prevents forward references across dict boundaries.

[
  # First dict: references @MyType before it's declared
  f: [fn@MyType [let x@Integer] x]
]

# Second dict: declares MyType
[
  MyType: [type Foo: [n: Integer]]
]

=== error
undefined type: MyType
